# Install xCAT Provisioner

{% include "provisioner/provisioner.md.j2" %}

This guide provisions compute nodes in **stateful** (*diskful*) mode: a base OS
is installed onto each node's local disk and the OpenHPC components are installed
in the same provisioning pass. Nodes keep their state across reboots. Following
the xCAT model, the OpenHPC package list and configuration are staged on the head
node and applied automatically by xCAT when each node installs and first boots --
there is no configuration over a live-node shell. The nodes are booted later, in
the deploy chapter.

